Root cause: the decoder loop skipped trailing bytes shorter than a full chunk
header, so a PNG truncated inside the IDAT chunk header reported "missing IDAT
chunk" instead of a truncation error, and a PNG without IEND was accepted.

Fix (in `verify/diff/diff.mjs`, before the passing rerun): the chunk loop now
iterates until end-of-buffer, throws `truncated PNG chunk header` on a partial
header, and requires a final `IEND` chunk (`missing IEND chunk`) for a valid
stream. Final passing run: `evidence/logs/F1-test.log`.
